  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Warm into Saturday, then cooling close to normal\nfor next week. A pattern shift and several systems may bring \nsome relief to the drought by early next week, as shower and \nthunderstorm chances increase.\n\nWe are currently in WNW flow aloft, with a weak upper level  \ndisturbance overhead and a trough at the surface along the Blue \nRidge. This combined with the heat of the day was triggering \nscattered showers over WV and parts of SW VA. Currently not\nseeing any lightning, but we may see a few strikes by this \nafternoon. QPF looks light and the little that does fall will do\nso over SE WV. Gusty westerly winds along with lower humidities\nsouth of Highway 460 will keep enhanced fire threat in that \narea through this evening.\n\nThe upper level pattern becomes even more meridional tomorrow,\nwith a tall mid level ridge extending from the Gulf coast into\ncentral Canada. This ridge along with high pressure at the \nsurface, rising heights, and southwesterly surface winds will \nsupport warm weather into the weekend. The ridging breaks down \nover the weekend, and we will be in busy zonal flow into the \nmiddle of next week with two deep bowling ball lows developing, \none over the intermountain west and one near Nova Scotia. \n\nThis increased upper level energy will mean several chances for \nrainfall with numerous surface boundaries in the area, namely \nover the weekend and again early next week. It appears the \natmosphere is trying to prime the pump so to speak, and if we \ndon't get rain on the first try or two, hopefully we will get \nsome early next week when a stronger system and much better \nmoisture will be in place. Forecaster experience along with \nBUFKIT soundings, persistence and Newton's First Law of Inertia \npoint towards low PoPs until at least Saturday, and maybe until \nthe early week system. \n\nIncreasing clouds and rain at times will mean temperatures much \ncloser to normal for this time of year beginning Sunday into \nnext week. While we may have some instability at times, only \ngeneral thunderstorms are expected.",
